From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:43:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770/hp39gii: boot to NSH on real hardware, keyboard
 input works

Hardware bring-up results for the HP 39gII (STMP3770, ARM926EJ-S).

Boot:
- arm_nommuhead.S: turn off the MMU/D-cache and clear the V bit (low
  vectors) at reset, and call arm_boot() before nx_start.  The SDP loader
  leaves CP15 in an unknown state.
- stmp3770_boot.c: stmp3770_copyvectors() used the I-cache invalidate
  "mcr p15,0,r0,c7,c5,4"; op2=4 is UNDEFINED on ARM926EJ-S and raised an
  Undefined exception on hardware (QEMU silently ignores it).  Use
  c7,c5,0 after a c7,c10,4 drain.  This was the fix that got the board
  from "hangs mid-boot" to an NSH prompt.
- Do not call stmp3770_clockconfig()/powerconfig() from arm_boot(): the
  BootROM has already set the PLLs up far enough, and reprogramming them
  during bring-up hangs the part.  The ExistOS-derived implementation is
  kept but not called.
- up_lowputc(): bound the TXFE poll.  The debug UART is not clocked on
  hardware, so the old unbounded loop could hang the boot forever.

LCD:
- LCDIF_PowerUp(): clear SFTRST|CLKGATE on the controller; on hardware it
  otherwise stays in reset and every write is silently dropped.
- Use the 24 MHz XTAL for PIXCLK (bypass) and fix the DMA channel
  enable/reset ordering.
- stmp3770_lcdcon.c: flush whole rows.  portDispFlushAreaBuf does x/3
  column addressing plus RMW for a non-multiple-of-3 start column, so the
  old per-glyph flush drew only the left part of every character.

Console:
- /dev/lcdcon now provides minimal terminal semantics.  readline does not
  echo ordinary characters itself (it expects the tty line discipline to
  do it) and CR->LF comes from ICRNL; on a bare char device input was read
  and silently dropped, which is why keys "did not work" on hardware.
  lcdcon_read() now echoes printable input, maps CR->LF and echoes the
  newline; putc() swallows ANSI escapes and implements ESC[K as
  erase-to-end-of-line.
- hp39gii_kbd.c: deliver keys only to /dev/lcdcon.  The KBD_ECHO path
  (polled PL011 up_putc) was never verified on hardware and is off.

Board:
- Initialise the panel synchronously when NSH uses /dev/lcdcon, and drop
  the bring-up self-test that ended in an infinite loop.
- nx_start.c: temporary stmp3770_stage() markers for LCD bisection.

Verified on hardware: NSH prompt on the LCD, keys echo, commands run.
